PROVENANCE
----------
The release apparatus lets anyone inspect exact-byte integrity, release-key
attribution, and timestamp status without relying only on repository prose:

  * provenance/sealed-commit.txt      — the sealed git commit + tree hash
  * provenance/sealed-commit.txt.ots  — detached OpenTimestamps proof; pending
                                        until trusted Bitcoin verification
  * a cryptographically SSH-signed git tag (provenance/allowed_signers)
  * an embedded provenance fingerprint in every skill file

These artifacts do not by themselves prove originality, legal authorship,
ownership, first creation, or infringement. See PROVENANCE.md for the full
threat model, what each layer does and does NOT prove, and the verification
procedure.

To verify everything from a clean clone:

    bash provenance/verify.sh
